{
    "background_story": "Sweetie was a pillar of the small town of Oakdale, known for her warm smile and unwavering conservative values. A lifelong Republican, she was a stalwart supporter of limited government and personal responsibility. As a young woman, Sweetie worked on several local campaigns, eventually becoming a respected voice in the community. She served as chairwoman of the Oakdale Republican Committee, helping to elect numerous candidates to office. Despite her strong convictions, Sweetie was beloved by people from both sides of the aisle for her kindness, generosity, and commitment to public service. Her annual Fourth of July BBQs were legendary, bringing together friends, family, and neighbors for a celebration of American values. Sweetie's legacy as a devoted public servant and proud Republican continues to inspire future generations.",
